# Audit report -- Phase 282: a lint that detects the defect four phases fixed by hand

**Verdict**: PASS
**Target**: docs/plan-qor-phase282-dialect-ownership-lint.md (iteration 9)
**Session**: 2026-09-09T0342-9a87f0
**Issues**: closes GH #469; makes GH #467 closable on disposition
**Mode**: adversarial; sixteen review rounds, independent reviewer, every load-bearing claim re-measured from source
**Iterations**: 9
**Risk Grade**: L2 -- one new advisory lint plus declaration-only edits to eight modules; no consumer behaviour changes

## Scope

Four sealed phases fixed the same defect by hand: a document field parsed by
more than one module, each with its own regex, diverging silently. Nothing
detected the next one. This adds the detector, advisory against a recorded
baseline, and it cannot fail a seal.

The design is inherited from Phase 276, parked unimplemented after four review
rounds (GH #469). Its property, declaration surface and baseline key are adopted
unchanged. The measurements were re-taken; three phases had landed since.

## Checklist

- [x] **Section 4 Razor** -- D1n is one four-step rule over two enumerated
      constructs, with "a third construct is a new plan" stated normatively
- [x] **No security stubs** -- declaration-only edits; no auth, security or PII path
- [x] **No ghost paths** -- emitter scope withdrawn (GH #468) with the
      measurement justifying it; the compliant class disclosed as synthetic-only
- [x] **Build path connected** -- `test_live_tree_matches_the_recorded_baseline`
      runs the lint against the real tree on every suite run, and D4 states that
      is the enforcement mechanism until promotion
- [x] **Merkle chain valid** -- `verify docs/META_LEDGER.md` OK through #774

## Measured, and confirmed by execution

| | pre-declaration | post-declaration |
|---|---|---|
| read-violation sites | 31 | 29 |
| (module, field) pairs | 10 | 8 |
| modules | 6 | 5 |
| `undeclared-label` | 1 | 1 |
| `false-declaration` | n/a | 1 |

Baseline artifact: **31 entries** on the five-part key
`module|document|field|kind|normalized-pattern`.

**D2's acceptance test closed by result.** D3 set it as the test of document
scoping: if scoping works, `meta_ledger_walker`'s rows vanish. Predicted 29,
returned 29, and the walker has 0 of 31 rows.

